# AI Agent Architecture

Use **specialized agents**, not one mega-prompt.

## Agents

| Agent | Role | Output |
|-------|------|--------|
| Repository Analyzer | Understand project structure | Stack detection JSON |
| Infrastructure Planner | Design topology | Architecture graph nodes/edges |
| Deployment Generator | Produce Zerops config | Valid zerops.yaml |
| Deployment Validator | Pre-flight checks | missing env, ports, Docker, deps |
| Log Analyst | Diagnose failures | Diagnosis (root cause, fix, confidence) |
| Optimization Advisor | Post-deploy review | Recommendations + deployment score |

## Structured Output

- Use tool/function calling with JSON schemas
- Validate LLM output with Pydantic before passing to services
- Keep prompts in `prompts/` — version and name by agent (e.g. `prompts/log-analyst.md`)

## Repository Detection Targets

Detect when present: language, framework, runtime version, package manager, database (Prisma/Postgres/etc.), frontend/backend split, workers, Redis, object storage needs.

## Log Analyst — Signature Feature

Transform raw logs into:

```
Root Cause: Prisma migration failed
Reason: DATABASE_URL missing
Impact: Backend cannot connect to database
Confidence: 96%
Suggested Fix: Set DATABASE_URL in Zerops env vars
```

Never return only "Exit code 1" — always explain in plain English.

## Deployment Score Dimensions

Security · Performance · Scalability · Reliability (0–10 scale with brief justification)
